    "title": "The Present Perfect",
    "subtitle": "Haber + past participle: forms, irregular participles and when Spain uses it instead of the preterite",
    "footer": "Spanish Learning Program · A2 · Verbs · Present perfect",
    "next": "Next: A2 · PDF 6 — Future and ongoing actions"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "After this PDF you can",
      "bullets": [
        "form the present perfect (he hablado, has comido, ha vivido) for every person",
        "use the regular and the irregular past participles (hecho, dicho, visto, escrito ...)",
        "talk about experiences, things you have or have not done yet, and the current week or year",
        "choose between the present perfect and the preterite, as it is done in Spain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "1. How it is formed"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The present perfect (<i>pretérito perfecto</i>) = the present tense of <b>haber</b> + the <b>past participle</b>. The participle never changes: it does not agree with the subject."
    },
    {
      "type": "conj",
      "tense": "present",
      "verb": "haber",
      "meaning": "to have (auxiliary verb)",
      "label": "irregular verb · only used as a helper here",
      "forms": [
        "*he*",
        "*has*",
        "*ha*",
        "*hemos*",
        "*habéis*",
        "*han*"
      ],
      "examples": [
        [
          "He terminado el trabajo.",
          "I have finished the work."
        ],
        [
          "¿Has visto mi móvil?",
          "Have you seen my phone?"
        ],
        [
          "Ella ha llegado tarde.",
          "She has arrived late."
        ],
        [
          "Hemos comido paella.",
          "We have eaten paella."
        ],
        [
          "¿Habéis estado en Sevilla?",
          "Have you (all) been to Seville?"
        ],
        [
          "Mis padres han salido.",
          "My parents have gone out."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "2. The past participle"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Take off -ar / -er / -ir and add <b>-ado</b> (for -ar) or <b>-ido</b> (for -er and -ir)."
    },
