    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "4. Word order"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "<b>He</b> and the participle are never separated: <i>Ya he comido. No he visto nada. Todavía no hemos terminado.</i>",
        "Negative: <b>no</b> goes before <b>he</b>: <i>No he comido.</i>",
        "Questions: <i>¿Has comido? ¿Ya has comido?</i>",
        "The participle does not change for gender or number: <i>Ellos han comido. Ella ha comido.</i> (Object pronouns go in front of haber: <i>Lo he visto</i>, see PDF 8.)"
      ]
    },
